title: Heartland state Assembly referendum
subtitle: How should we campaign against the referendum?
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1931 and month >= 7 and landtag_ref_signatures_passed
on-arrival: landtag_ref_collectivist = 1 if collectivist_relation < 40 and not collectivist_leader == "Conciliators"; landtag_ref_collectivist = 0 if collectivist_relation >= 40 or collectivist_leader == "Conciliators"; pro_republic += 3 if not landtag_ref_collectivist; pro_republic -= 3 if landtag_ref_collectivist
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/social_fascist.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}
max-visits: 1

= Heartland state Assembly referendum

[? if landtag_ref_collectivist: The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> has reversed its position and now supports the referendum! It’s astonishing that the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, which labels us <span style="color: #c00000;">social</span> <span style="color: #7A3C00;">fascists</span>, is now collaborating with [+ royalist_leader +] and Mallin. They have rebranded the referendum as the "red plebiscite" following an unacceptable ultimatum to the Heartland government. The <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span> have mobilized so extensively that many now believe they have "taken the lead" in directing the campaign from the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>. ?][? if not landtag_ref_collectivist: Fortunately, the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>[? if collectivist_leader == "Halsmark": &nbsp;despite its <span style="color: #c00000;">social</span> <span style="color: #7A3C00;">fascist</span> stance toward us,?] has refrained from taking a position on the referendum. The relatively low signature count of only [+ landtag_ref_signatures +]% is a positive sign, making a victory for the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> highly unlikely. ?]

[? if landtag_ref_collectivist: The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>’s newfound support for the referendum has dramatically altered the situation, crushing earlier optimism stemming from the low number of signatures gathered in the first phase. Fortunately, many <span style="color: #700000;">**Communist**</span> workers are disgusted by the "<span style="color: #700000;">red</span>-<span style="color: #7A3C00;">brown</span>" plebiscite. Likewise, many <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> voters are reluctant to cast their ballots in alignment with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Communists**</span>.?][? if not landtag_ref_collectivist: Even though this referendum is doomed to fail, it still provides the Commonwealth Right with an opportunity to deepen political polarization, as evidenced by the anti-democratic rightwards shift of the bourgeois parties.?]

With our control of the Heartland government, we can campaign using state resources.

- @do_campaign: Let’s review our campaign options.
- @no_campaign: We shouldn't allocate resources to this.

@do_campaign

We have a variety of options to choose from.

- @bourgeois
- @communist_prussia
- @media
- @urge_paramilitary
- @kpd
- @hope: We have done enough.
- @no_campaign_2: We shouldn't allocate resources to this.

@bourgeois
title: Request assistance from our coalition partners.
view-if: marcher_heartland and not bourgeois_campaign_landtag
choose-if: not in_popular_front_heartland and not in_left_front_heartland and unionist_relation >= 50
unavailable-subtitle: [? if in_popular_front_heartland or in_left_front_heartland: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] sees no reason to intervene in saving the incumbent government. ?] [? if unionist_relation < 50: We lack sufficient relations with the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. ?]
on-arrival: pro_republic += 3; faithful_royalist -= 4; faithful_unionist += 3; faithful_marcher += 1; unionist_relation += 3; gold_relation += 3; ddp_relation += 3; ddp_left += 2; ddp_cohesion += 2; gold_left += 3; bourgeois_campaign_landtag = 1
face-image: img/weimar_coalition.jpg
go-to: do_campaign

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] has joined our efforts with its own propaganda campaign, doing their part in targeting Catholics and urging them to stay home.

@communist_prussia
title: Request assistance from the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.
subtitle: The bourgeois parties will not be pleased by our cooperation.
view-if: marcher_heartland and not landtag_ref_collectivist and not communist_campaign_landtag
choose-if: in_popular_front_heartland or in_left_front_heartland
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span> sees no reason to intervene in saving a government in which they have no involvement.
on-arrival: pro_republic += 3; commons_collectivist += 2; commons_marcher += 2; commons_royalist -= 2; disfavored_royalist -= 4; disfavored_collectivist += 4; collectivist_relation += 10; unionist_relation -= 5; gold_relation -= 5; ddp_relation -= 3; ddp_right += 2; ddp_cohesion -= 2; gold_right += 5; communist_campaign_landtag = 1
face-image: img/kpd_march.jpg
go-to: do_campaign

Great news! The <span style="color: #D50000;">Comintern</span> has approved the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>'s participation in our propaganda campaign against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>.

However, this display of left-wing unity has frightened the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and <span style="color: #D3C24D;">liberals</span>, with some even choosing to support the referendum to protest.

@media
title: Use Vorwärts and our radio stations to broadcast against the plebiscite.
subtitle: -1 resource
view-if: not radio_campaign_landtag
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; burgher_marcher += (radio + commercialized_media); guild_marcher += (radio + commercialized_media); commons_marcher += campaign_media; disfavored_marcher += campaign_media; burgher_royalist -= (radio + commercialized_media); guild_royalist -= (radio + commercialized_media); commons_royalist -= campaign_media; disfavored_royalist -= campaign_media; socialism += 3; nationalism -= 1; nationalism -= 2 if pacifism > 1; pro_republic += (radio + commercialized_media); radio_campaign_landtag = 1
face-image: img/vorwarts_2.jpg
go-to: do_campaign

The effect of this campaign depends on the strength of our already established media empire. [? if commercialized_media: Our commercialized newspapers and radio stations have been effective in persuading the middle classes to stay home. ?][? if radio: Our radio station has played a crucial role in reaching middle-class voters. ?][? if campaign_media: The widespread presence of <span style="color: #c00000;">socialist</span> propaganda among the working-class has helped sway some to our side. ?]

@urge_paramilitary
view-if: not political_decree_landtag_2 and political_decree == 1 and chancellor == "Askew" and marcher_toleration
choose-if: marcher_heartland and unionist_relation >= 35
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not marcher_heartland: We don't control the Heartland government. ?] [? if unionist_relation < 35: We lack sufficient relations with Askew. ?]
title: Urge Askew to pass a second decree against "political excesses", further restricting press freedoms.
on-arrival: political_decree += 1; heartland_police_loyalty += 0.04; heartland_police_strength += 5; collectivist_relation -= 6; vanguard_militancy *= 0.9; vanguard_strength *= 0.85; loyalist_militancy *= 0.96; loyalist_strength *= 0.96; warden_militancy *= 0.98; warden_strength *= 0.98; commons_collectivist -= 2; commons_royalist -= 2; disfavored_collectivist -= 4; disfavored_royalist -= 4; burgher_royalist -= 3; dufour_angry_bruning += 5; political_decree_landtag_2 = 1
face-image: img/stahlhelm_poster.jpg
go-to: do_campaign

Carl Heath and Otto Bristol have successfully persuaded Askew to issue another emergency decree, forcing 2,500 newspapers—regardless of their political stance or position on the plebiscite—to publish a government statement urging the public to abstain from voting.

This decision has further inflamed the already volatile political climate, prompting President DuFour to promise a review of the decree following strong backlash from the supporters of Mallin and Gallax.

@kpd
title: We will attempt to cause a general strike of <span style="color: #700000;">**Communist**</span> voters.
subtitle: -1 resource
view-if: landtag_ref_collectivist and not collectivist_campaign_landtag
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; commons_collectivist -= 2; commons_royalist -= 1; commons_marcher += 3; disfavored_collectivist -= 3; disfavored_royalist -= 1; disfavored_marcher += 4; pro_republic += 4; collectivist_relation -= 15; gold_left += 1; ddp_left += 1; ddp_cohesion += 1; collectivist_campaign_landtag = 1
face-image: img/red-brown.jpg
go-to: do_campaign

Pointing out the obvious always helps, even some <span style="color: #8B0000;">**RFB**</span> men are disgusted by their own party collaborating with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">fascists</span>. 

@hope
view-if: collectivist_campaign_landtag or political_decree_landtag_2 or radio_campaign_landtag or communist_campaign_landtag or bourgeois_campaign_landtag

We can only hope for the best.

@no_campaign_2
view-if: not collectivist_campaign_landtag and not political_decree_landtag_2 and not radio_campaign_landtag and not communist_campaign_landtag and not bourgeois_campaign_landtag
on-arrival: commons_marcher -= 3; guild_marcher -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 3; commons_royalist += 3; burgher_royalist += 3; guild_royalist += 3; pro_republic -= 5; faithful_marcher -= 2; faithful_royalist += 2; commons_collectivist += 3; disfavored_marcher -= 5; disfavored_royalist += 5; disfavored_collectivist += 3;

The referendum is likely going to fail with or without our presence in the campaign. However, anti-democratic sentiment is inflamed, and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> is using our silence to spread their radicalizing propaganda to the people.

@no_campaign
on-arrival: commons_marcher -= 3; guild_marcher -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 3; commons_royalist += 3; burgher_royalist += 3; guild_royalist += 3; pro_republic -= 5; faithful_marcher -= 2; faithful_royalist += 2; commons_collectivist += 3; disfavored_marcher -= 5; disfavored_royalist += 5; disfavored_collectivist += 3;

The referendum is likely going to fail with or without our presence in the campaign. However, anti-democratic sentiment is inflamed, and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> is using our silence to spread their radicalizing propaganda to the people.